{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846868-alternate-names-for-the-clans","id":846868,"title":"Alternate Names for the Clans","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-13T18:58:11-07:00","id":846868,"title":"Alternate Names for the Clans","content":"Does anyone have alternate names for the five clans that they're especially fond of? I've never liked that Ventrue, Gangrel, and Nosferatu have been inherited from oWoD, and both Daeva and Mekhet have ties to human cultures that I don't think fits the broader, universal concept of the clans that Requiem supports. It gets especially odd in Requiem for Rome, when only one clan has a Roman name and the rest have associations with mortal ethnic groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T19:23:09-07:00","id":846875,"title":"","content":"In my VTR setting the australian supernaturals has the following nicknames for the clans:<br /> <br /> Daeva, redbellies/davos<br /> Gangrel, dingos/gangs<br /> Mekhet, redbacks/kets<br /> Nosferatu, bluebottles/grubs<br /> Ventrue, galahs/ventos","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T01:28:06-07:00","id":846972,"title":"","content":"For the Age of Azar setting I and several others are working on, we worked a few alternative names for some of the Clans (and even made an entirely new one) to fit with the setting. <hr /><br /> Daeva<br /> Gangrel (Habiru)<br /> Mekhet<br /> Nosferatu (Ushabti)<br /> Ventrue (Mumvuri)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T09:45:17-07:00","id":847142,"title":"","content":"You could just use their nicknames. Serpents, Savages, Shadows, Haunts, and Lords.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T13:59:38-07:00","id":847292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846868-alternate-names-for-the-clans?p=847142#post847142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could just use their nicknames. Serpents, Savages, Shadows, Haunts, and Lords.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is what I do. I almost never use the formal names, only nicknames. I still use succubus/incubus and Worm for names as well. I use Feral instead of Savage as well. Kingmakers and Know-it-alls for Ven and Mehket. <br /> <br /> Most formal names I use I reserve for bloodlines and lineages. Clan names are used by the Ordo as a kind of &quot;scientific nomenclature&quot; that's not in common usage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T15:35:07-07:00","id":847339,"title":"","content":"These are the names I used for a campaign set in ancient Athens:<br /> <br /> <b>Siskioi</b> (Mekhet)<br /> <b>Empusae</b> (Daeva)<br /> <b>Vrihi</b> (influenced by the True Brujah from VtM)<br /> <b>Erinyes</b> (Strix)<br /> <b>Lamia</b> (A lost clan from Libya which first developed Dominate, later stolen by the Julii)<br /> <b>Nosophoroi</b> (Nosferatu)<br /> <b>Maniae</b> (Malkavians)<br /> <br /> The Gangrel were not named on purpose. Were they any different from Lupines and the Draugr? Perhaps, but the Eupatridae did not care to find out. Only the Kerberoi were allowed inside their Polis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T18:24:04-07:00","id":847445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846868-alternate-names-for-the-clans#post846868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have alternate names for the five clans that they're especially fond of? I've never liked that Ventrue, Gangrel, and Nosferatu have been inherited from oWoD, and both Daeva and Mekhet have ties to human cultures that I don't think fits the broader, universal concept of the clans that Requiem supports. It gets especially odd in Requiem for Rome, when only one clan has a Roman name and the rest have associations with mortal ethnic groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue the Mekhet and Daeva actually fit better in the Roman setting name wise.<br /> <br /> I use Neferatu (or something like it)in modern setting which is either romanian for afflicted or Demon for the Haunts.<br /> The nos even make fun of Stoker for inventing the word Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> Ven for Ventru for a formal for the Lords<br /> <br /> I assume the nicknames are the universal Names in various languages and the Formal names change over time.<br /> Nicknames:Shadows, Haunts , Serpents/Succubus, Savage/beasts, Lords/Tyrants<br /> <br /> Their proper names change over time with cultures.<br /> <br /> Addendum:<span style=\"color:#000000\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> necuratul ('the devil') and nesuferitul ('insufferable one</span></span><span style=\"color:#CCCCCC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">')</span></span><br /> <i>necurat</i><span style=\"color:#29303B\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"> (&quot;unclean&quot;, usually associated with the occult) and </span></span><i>nesuferit</i><span style=\"color:#29303B\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"> (&quot;insufferable&quot;</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","user":"Chattnos","date":". 03-14-2016, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T23:59:44-07:00","id":850441,"title":"","content":"Some thoughts on Clan names for <i>Requiem For Rome</i>:<br /> <br /> Daeva: Many Daeva deliberately cultivate an aura of exoticism and transgression, and would have no problem using a foreign name. For those who prefer to integrate into the society of the Roman dead, Succubus probably wouldn't carry the right meaning in the Latin of Late Antiquity (referring to a strumpet or mistress rather than a supernatural being), but <b>Incubo</b> (plural <b>I</b><b>ncubones</b>) would be a period- appropriate title, and might be rendered feminine with the ad-hoc form <b>Incuba</b>. On the other hand, a somewhat more neutral term might be <b>Chaldaei</b>, &quot;Chaldeans,&quot; referring to their presumptive geographical origin. <br /> <br /> Gangrel: <b>Barbari</b> seems like the most straightforward term, meaning &quot;foreigner&quot; or &quot;savage,&quot; though <b>Feri</b>, &quot;wild animals,&quot; could be a particularly derogatory variant. For Gangrel who have more successfully integrated into Roman society, <b>Foederati</b> may be an appropriate name, being borrowed from the term the Empire uses to refer to barbarian allies hired to fight with the legions, many of whom were subsequently allowed to settle within the Empire.<br /> <br /> Mekhet: <b>Umbrae</b> means &quot;shadows,&quot; but can also mean &quot;ghosts,&quot; which seems like an appropriate native term for the Mekhet. Alternately, you could go with <b>Taciti</b>, roughly &quot;the silent ones&quot; or &quot;the secret ones.&quot; <br /> <br /> Nosferatu: <b>Virmes</b>, &quot;Worms,&quot; seems most appropriate, as it is, as I recall, pretty consistently the term that gets used for them in the setting.<br /> <br /> The Julii obviously already have a period-specific name, and the Ventrue either aren't around or are keeping a very low profile, so they likely don't have any one well-known name in Latin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T08:32:00-07:00","id":850572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846868-alternate-names-for-the-clans?p=850441#post850441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some thoughts on Clan names for <i>Requiem For Rome</i>:<br /> <br /> Daeva: Many Daeva deliberately cultivate an aura of exoticism and transgression, and would have no problem using a foreign name. For those who prefer to integrate into the society of the Roman dead, Succubus probably wouldn't carry the right meaning in the Latin of Late Antiquity (referring to a strumpet or mistress rather than a supernatural being), but <b>Incubo</b> (plural <b>I</b><b>ncubones</b>) would be a period- appropriate title, and might be rendered feminine with the ad-hoc form <b>Incuba</b>. On the other hand, a somewhat more neutral term might be <b>Chaldaei</b>, &amp;quot;Chaldeans,&amp;quot; referring to their presumptive geographical origin.</div> </div> </div> </div>As of Second Edition modern nickname for Daeva is Serpents, not Succubi. In Rome, their nickname was Courtesans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846868-alternate-names-for-the-clans?p=850441#post850441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gangrel: <b>Barbari</b> seems like the most straightforward term, meaning &amp;quot;foreigner&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;savage,&amp;quot; though <b>Feri</b>, &amp;quot;wild animals,&amp;quot; could be a particularly derogatory variant. For Gangrel who have more successfully integrated into Roman society, <b>Foederati</b> may be an appropriate name, being borrowed from the term the Empire uses to refer to barbarian allies hired to fight with the legions, many of whom were subsequently allowed to settle within the Empire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their official RfR nickname is Wanderers, but I think I like your suggestion better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846868-alternate-names-for-the-clans?p=850441#post850441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mekhet: <b>Umbrae</b> means &amp;quot;shadows,&amp;quot; but can also mean &amp;quot;ghosts,&amp;quot; which seems like an appropriate native term for the Mekhet. Alternately, you could go with <b>Taciti</b>, roughly &amp;quot;the silent ones&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;the secret ones.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>In RfR, they're called the Seers, which I've always found more appropriate than Shadows, given that their signature Discipline is more about uncovering information than keeping themselves hidden, and even Obfuscate is a means to an end for most Mekhet. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846868-alternate-names-for-the-clans?p=850441#post850441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nosferatu: <b>Virmes</b>, &amp;quot;Worms,&amp;quot; seems most appropriate, as it is, as I recall, pretty consistently the term that gets used for them in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worms is their official nickname in RfR, yeah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846868-alternate-names-for-the-clans?p=850441#post850441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Julii obviously already have a period-specific name, and the Ventrue either aren't around or are keeping a very low profile, so they likely don't have any one well-known name in Latin.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Julii's nickname is The Founders. There don't seem to be many (open) Ventrue in Rome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T11:15:56-07:00","id":850698,"title":"","content":"Interesting; I guess I should have pulled out RfR and checked the nicknames.<br /> <br /> Looking at Roman terms for prostitutes and other objects of sexual desire, the most appropriate equivalent to &quot;courtesan&quot; might be <b>Concubinus</b> for men and <b>Concubina</b> for women. However, while a concubina could be a free woman and was afforded legal protections by the mortal government of Rome, a concubinus was almost always a slave. Indeed, there's really no delicate way to refer to a male &quot;courtesan&quot; in Latin, but <b>Ganymedes </b>(singular and plural would be identical), after the mythological figure, might be an appropriate euphemism. Another appropriate term for a female courtesan might be <b>Meretrix</b>, literally &quot;she who earns.&quot;<br /> <br /> There are, likewise, a number of possible terms for a &quot;seer&quot; in Latin, but because &quot;Augur&quot; is an official title in the Camarilla, the most appropriate term for the Mekhet might be <b>Python</b> (plural <b>Pythones</b>), which refers to an oracle or soothsayer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T19:48:37-07:00","id":851537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846868-alternate-names-for-the-clans?p=850572#post850572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As of Second Edition modern nickname for Daeva is Serpents, not Succubi.</div> </div> </div> </div>What was the reason for this, do you know?<br /> Oddly enough Serpents fits their old weakness to me while Succubi fits the waton curse better.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T20:37:33-07:00","id":851553,"title":"","content":"Just guessing. But the nicknames are from a vampire's point of view. Vampires dealing with a daeva who succumb to their weakness wouldn't see succubi, they would see vampires who could potentially feel an interest in kine that could overcome the bonds of the All Night Society. Potentially untrustworthy, as an outsider to their clan, you can't be entirely sure where their loyalties lie.<br /> <br /> Of course I'm notoriously bad at these things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T21:01:22-07:00","id":851565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846868-alternate-names-for-the-clans?p=851537#post851537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was the reason for this, do you know?<br /> Oddly enough Serpents fits their old weakness to me while Succubi fits the waton curse better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really have any special insight into this matter, your guess is as good as mine. It may have had to do with de-emphasizing the sexual aspect? Though as you observed, their new Bane kind of relies on feeding as a metaphor for sex more heavily than the old weakness, so this reason seems unlikely. Maybe to make the nickname more gender-neutral, since technically succubi is specifically female and incubi is the male equivalent. I'm really not sure. I will say, I like Serpents better, whatever the reason for the change may have been.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-23-2016, 01:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}